From: Plain Browser
Subject: [safebrowsing] Treat SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC as a phishing list in GetThreatSeverity

Category: 70-safebrowsing. Applies after 0003 (same file). Since 0004 the phishing list is synced as
SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC, so a local prefix hit reaches GetThreatSeverity() with that type, which upstream
lists under NOTREACHED(). In the official build that is a fatal crash of the browser process (seen 2026-11-04 in
0.1.5.0: "sb_local_database_manager.cc:171 NOTREACHED hit. Unexpected ThreatType encountered: 2"). It gets the
same severity as SOCIAL_ENGINEERING.
---
--- a/components/safe_browsing/core/browser/db/sb_local_database_manager.cc
+++ b/components/safe_browsing/core/browser/db/sb_local_database_manager.cc
@@ -149,6 +149,9 @@
   switch (list_id.threat_type()) {
     case MALWARE_THREAT:
     case SOCIAL_ENGINEERING:
+    // Plain Browser: the phishing list is synced as SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC
+    // (patch 0004), so a prefix hit reports that type; same severity.
+    case SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC:
     case MALICIOUS_BINARY:
       return 0;
     case UNWANTED_SOFTWARE:
@@ -166,7 +169,6 @@
     case CLIENT_INCIDENT:
     case CSD_DOWNLOAD_ALLOWLIST:
     case POTENTIALLY_HARMFUL_APPLICATION:
-    case SOCIAL_ENGINEERING_PUBLIC:
     case THREAT_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED:
       NOTREACHED() << "Unexpected ThreatType encountered: "
                    << list_id.threat_type();
